# What the daily-web deployment actually needs.
#
# The Vercel project's Root Directory is `web`. Without this file the CLI
# uploads 1.8 GB of virtualenv, Xcode project and local caches to build a
# static site, which is slow enough to time out.
#
# `/backend` used to be excluded outright, under the heading "nothing else in
# this repository takes part". That stopped being true when the Lab gained
# functions that read the case suite at runtime, and the way it announced
# itself was a preview build failing on `cannot stage
# backend/lab/__init__.py: it does not exist`. The exclusion is now
# file-by-file rather than wholesale: `scripts/stage-lab-evidence.ts` names
# exactly what a deployed function reads, and this names the same set. A test
# asserts the two lists agree, because two hand-maintained lists that must
# match are two lists that will not.

/Daily
/DailyTests
/DailyUITests
/Daily.xcodeproj
/scripts
/docs
/.context
/.conductor
/.github
/.claude

# Everything under backend/, except the evidence the Lab functions stage.
# A parent directory cannot be re-included once excluded, hence the walk.
/backend/*
!/backend/lab
!/backend/app
/backend/lab/*
!/backend/lab/__init__.py
!/backend/lab/harness.py
!/backend/lab/cases
!/backend/lab/contract
/backend/lab/contract/*
!/backend/lab/contract/versions
/backend/app/*
!/backend/app/services
/backend/app/services/*
!/backend/app/services/openai_service.py
!/backend/app/services/ranking_contract.py
